{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787530712423,"sessionID":"ses_fcede7034ffedO3qY1epZkSTJa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-96dbfa188b1bae2a","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-EwI6KY/checkout/app/trade-capture/domain/calculations.ts"},"output":"<path>/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-EwI6KY/checkout/app/trade-capture/domain/calculations.ts</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: import type { DeskSummary, Side, Trade, TradeEconomics } from \"./types.ts\";\n2: \n3: export function withinOneCent(left: number, right: number): boolean {\n4:   return Math.abs(Math.round(left * 100) - Math.round(right * 100)) <= 1;\n5: }\n6: \n7: export function calculateEconomics(\n8:   originalFace: number,\n9:   factor: number,\n10:   price: number,\n11:   side: Side,\n12: ): TradeEconomics {\n13:   const currentFace = originalFace * factor;\n14:   const grossPrincipal = currentFace * price / 100;\n15:   return {\n16:     currentFace,\n17:     grossPrincipal,\n18:     signedExposure: side === \"buy\" ? grossPrincipal : -grossPrincipal,\n19:   };\n20: }\n21: \n22: export function summarizeDesk(trades: readonly Trade[]): DeskSummary {\n23:   const active = trades.filter((trade) => trade.status !== \"cancelled\");\n24:   const buyExposure = active.reduce(\n25:     (sum, trade) => sum + Math.max(0, trade.economics.signedExposure),\n26:     0,\n27:   );\n28:   const sellExposure = active.reduce(\n29:     (sum, trade) => sum + Math.min(0, trade.economics.signedExposure),\n30:     0,\n31:   );\n32:   return {\n33:     activeTradeCount: active.length,\n34:     bookedTradeCount: active.filter((trade) => trade.status === \"booked\").length,\n35:     exceptionCount: active.reduce(\n36:       (sum, trade) => sum + trade.exceptions.filter((item) => item.severity === \"error\").length,\n37:       0,\n38:     ),\n39:     buyExposure,\n40:     sellExposure,\n41:     netExposure: buyExposure + sellExposure,\n42:     grossPrincipal: active.reduce(\n43:       (sum, trade) => sum + Math.abs(trade.economics.signedExposure),\n44:       0,\n45:     ),\n46:   };\n47: }\n\n(End of file - total 47 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"import type { DeskSummary, Side, Trade, TradeEconomics } from \"./types.ts\";\n\nexport function withinOneCent(left: number, right: number): boolean {\n  return Math.abs(Math.round(left * 100) - Math.round(right * 100)) <= 1;\n}\n\nexport function calculateEconomics(\n  originalFace: number,\n  factor: number,\n  price: number,\n  side: Side,\n): TradeEconomics {\n  const currentFace = originalFace * factor;\n  const grossPrincipal = currentFace * price / 100;\n  return {\n    currentFace,\n    grossPrincipal,\n    signedExposure: side === \"buy\" ? grossPrincipal : -grossPrincipal,\n  };\n}","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-EwI6KY/checkout/app/trade-capture/domain/calculations.ts","text":"import type { DeskSummary, Side, Trade, TradeEconomics } from \"./types.ts\";\n\nexport function withinOneCent(left: number, right: number): boolean {\n  return Math.abs(Math.round(left * 100) - Math.round(right * 100)) <= 1;\n}\n\nexport function calculateEconomics(\n  originalFace: number,\n  factor: number,\n  price: number,\n  side: Side,\n): TradeEconomics {\n  const currentFace = originalFace * factor;\n  const grossPrincipal = currentFace * price / 100;\n  return {\n    currentFace,\n    grossPrincipal,\n    signedExposure: side === \"buy\" ? grossPrincipal : -grossPrincipal,\n  };\n}\n\nexport function summarizeDesk(trades: readonly Trade[]): DeskSummary {\n  const active = trades.filter((trade) => trade.status !== \"cancelled\");\n  const buyExposure = active.reduce(\n    (sum, trade) => sum + Math.max(0, trade.economics.signedExposure),\n    0,\n  );\n  const sellExposure = active.reduce(\n    (sum, trade) => sum + Math.min(0, trade.economics.signedExposure),\n    0,\n  );\n  return {\n    activeTradeCount: active.length,\n    bookedTradeCount: active.filter((trade) => trade.status === \"booked\").length,\n    exceptionCount: active.reduce(\n      (sum, trade) => sum + trade.exceptions.filter((item) => item.severity === \"error\").length,\n      0,\n    ),\n    buyExposure,\n    sellExposure,\n    netExposure: buyExposure + sellExposure,\n    grossPrincipal: active.reduce(\n      (sum, trade) => sum + Math.abs(trade.economics.signedExposure),\n      0,\n    ),\n  };\n}","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":47,"totalLines":47,"truncated":false}},"title":"app/trade-capture/domain/calculations.ts","time":{"start":1787530712409,"end":1787530712420}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Alright, let me check the product brief — the T7-trade-capture-plan task, and if needed, the calculations file too (to understand the sign convention, e.g., how sellExposure is calculated). Also, to make sure I'm not breaking lint, I'll check the lint rules (eslint config) and typecheck scripts in package.json as well.\n","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_031220fbd001In1FBEpVz7FziL","sessionID":"ses_fcede7034ffedO3qY1epZkSTJa","messageID":"msg_03121f5f5001O2P2b7yiifv3V5"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1787530714064,"sessionID":"ses_fcede7034ffedO3qY1epZkSTJa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9d07bbcdc488ab60","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-EwI6KY/checkout/benchmark/tasks/T7-trade-capture-plan/prompt.md"},"output":"<path>/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-EwI6KY/checkout/benchmark/tasks/T7-trade-capture-plan/prompt.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Read-only architecture task\n2: \n3: Plan the implementation of the securitized-product trade capture mock described\n4: in `benchmark/projects/T7-securitized-trade-capture/PRODUCT.md`.\n5: \n6: Inspect the existing application structure, package scripts, TypeScript setup,\n7: and test approach before proposing files. This is a read-only task. Do not edit,\n8: create, rename, or delete files. Do not use the network, install dependencies,\n9: change Git state, start a service, or inspect `benchmark/private` or\n10: `benchmark/runs`.\n11: \n12: The implementation must be divided across four bounded workers:\n13: \n14: 1. Codex + GPT-5.6 Terra for domain types, calculations, validation, seed data,\n15:    and domain tests.\n16: 2. Claude Code + Sonnet 5 for the accessible trade-ticket component.\n17: 3. OpenCode + Qwen3.8-27B for a small desk-insights component.\n18: 4. OpenCode + Kimi K3 for application state, blotter, selected-trade review,\n19:    and visual system.\n20: \n21: Codex + GPT-5.6 Sol will integrate. Claude Code + Opus 5 will review the plan\n22: and later review the completed application.\n23: \n24: Return a concise report with these exact sections:\n25: \n26: ## Product interpretation\n27: \n28: State the workflow and the most important simplifying assumptions.\n29: \n30: ## Architecture\n31: \n32: Define the route, client/server boundary, state ownership, domain module, and\n33: component tree.\n34: \n35: ## Stable contracts\n36: \n37: Specify exact exported TypeScript types, functions, and component props that\n38: must be frozen before worker execution.\n39: \n40: ## File ownership\n41: \n42: Give each of the four implementation workers an explicit, non-overlapping list\n43: of owned files. Identify the small set of integrator-owned files.\n44: \n45: ## Worker tasks\n46: \n47: For each worker, give the acceptance requirements, commands it may run, and\n48: what it must not change.\n49: \n50: ## Integration sequence\n51: \n52: Explain how Sol should combine the four patches and how to handle an interface\n53: mismatch without hiding a worker failure.\n54: \n55: ## Verification\n56: \n57: Define domain tests, type checking, lint, build, rendered-HTML assertions, and\n58: manual checks. Separate checks that can run in isolated worker branches from the\n59: final integrated gate.\n60: \n61: ## Risks and review focus\n62: \n63: List the five most important domain or engineering risks for the Opus reviewer.\n64: \n65: Keep the report below 1,800 words. Cite concrete repository paths for claims\n66: about the existing application.\n\n(End of file - total 66 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Read-only architecture task\n\nPlan the implementation of the securitized-product trade capture mock described\nin `benchmark/projects/T7-securitized-trade-capture/PRODUCT.md`.\n\nInspect the existing application structure, package scripts, TypeScript setup,\nand test approach before proposing files. This is a read-only task. Do not edit,\ncreate, rename, or delete files. Do not use the network, install dependencies,\nchange Git state, start a service, or inspect `benchmark/private` or\n`benchmark/runs`.\n\nThe implementation must be divided across four bounded workers:\n\n1. Codex + GPT-5.6 Terra for domain types, calculations, validation, seed data,\n   and domain tests.\n2. Claude Code + Sonnet 5 for the accessible trade-ticket component.\n3. OpenCode + Qwen3.8-27B for a small desk-insights component.\n4. OpenCode + Kimi K3 for application state, blotter, selected-trade review,\n   and visual system.\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-EwI6KY/checkout/benchmark/tasks/T7-trade-capture-plan/prompt.md","text":"# Read-only architecture task\n\nPlan the implementation of the securitized-product trade capture mock described\nin `benchmark/projects/T7-securitized-trade-capture/PRODUCT.md`.\n\nInspect the existing application structure, package scripts, TypeScript setup,\nand test approach before proposing files. This is a read-only task. Do not edit,\ncreate, rename, or delete files. Do not use the network, install dependencies,\nchange Git state, start a service, or inspect `benchmark/private` or\n`benchmark/runs`.\n\nThe implementation must be divided across four bounded workers:\n\n1. Codex + GPT-5.6 Terra for domain types, calculations, validation, seed data,\n   and domain tests.\n2. Claude Code + Sonnet 5 for the accessible trade-ticket component.\n3. OpenCode + Qwen3.8-27B for a small desk-insights component.\n4. OpenCode + Kimi K3 for application state, blotter, selected-trade review,\n   and visual system.\n\nCodex + GPT-5.6 Sol will integrate. Claude Code + Opus 5 will review the plan\nand later review the completed application.\n\nReturn a concise report with these exact sections:\n\n## Product interpretation\n\nState the workflow and the most important simplifying assumptions.\n\n## Architecture\n\nDefine the route, client/server boundary, state ownership, domain module, and\ncomponent tree.\n\n## Stable contracts\n\nSpecify exact exported TypeScript types, functions, and component props that\nmust be frozen before worker execution.\n\n## File ownership\n\nGive each of the four implementation workers an explicit, non-overlapping list\nof owned files. Identify the small set of integrator-owned files.\n\n## Worker tasks\n\nFor each worker, give the acceptance requirements, commands it may run, and\nwhat it must not change.\n\n## Integration sequence\n\nExplain how Sol should combine the four patches and how to handle an interface\nmismatch without hiding a worker failure.\n\n## Verification\n\nDefine domain tests, type checking, lint, build, rendered-HTML assertions, and\nmanual checks. Separate checks that can run in isolated worker branches from the\nfinal integrated gate.\n\n## Risks and review focus\n\nList the five most important domain or engineering risks for the Opus reviewer.\n\nKeep the report below 1,800 words. Cite concrete repository paths for claims\nabout the existing application.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":66,"totalLines":66,"truncated":false}},"title":"benchmark/tasks/T7-trade-capture-plan/prompt.md","time":{"start":1787530714054,"end":1787530714061}},"id":"prt_031221640001fd0BrJ9crxzAv2","sessionID":"ses_fcede7034ffedO3qY1epZkSTJa","messageID":"msg_03121f5f5001O2P2b7yiifv3V5"}}
